# Instructions for clauded sessions
#
# Copy this file to ~/.clauded/home/AGENTS.md and edit it.
#
# That directory is the container's home, so every clauded session reads this as
# its project instructions. Sessions running on your Mac never see it. Claude Code
# picks AGENTS.md up on its own; no symlink is needed.
#
# Record what is true only inside the container, so a session does not have to
# discover it by failing first.

## This session runs in a Docker container

The working directory, ~/dev and ~/.claude are shared with the Mac. Everything
else is the container's own and resets when the session ends.

## Tools that live on the Mac

Tools installed on the Mac with Homebrew are absent here. Where a container
replacement exists, name it and say which to use:

- `pbcopy` / `pbpaste` work: they forward to the Mac's clipboard.
- `open` works through `xdg-open`, opening in the Mac's browser.
- `<your-mac-tool>` is not installed. Use `<container-equivalent>` instead.

## Tools added to the image

Anything installed through ~/.clauded/custom/Dockerfile is available here. List
what it provides so a session knows to reach for it.
